From 56bc7fdeb48a923fef9416f36984e71597ff3fae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Grasso <me@leonardograsso.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:28:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(mermaid-text): draw decisions as a shallow diamond

Box-drawing diagonals are as steep as a cell is tall, so a decision node read as a box with odd corners. Decisions are now drawn with one-eighth horizontal lines from the Symbols for Legacy Computing block, climbing from the row ends to the centre, with flat one-eighth vertical ends on the middle row. A diamond is at least 17 columns wide so its outline rises at most one eighth of a row per column; arrow tips on the outline survive the redraw.
